['```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>

void modifyVector(std::vector<int>& vec, int targetValue, int replacementValue, int insertionIndex) {
    // Check for edge cases
    if (vec.empty()) { 
        if(insertionIndex == 0){
            vec.push_back(replacementValue);
        }
        return;
    }
    if (insertionIndex > vec.size()) { 
        insertionIndex = vec.size();
    }

    // Find the first occurrence of target value
    auto it = std::find(vec.begin(), vec.end(), targetValue);

    if(it != vec.end()){
        *it = replacementValue;  // Replace the target value
    }else{
        vec.insert(vec.begin() + insertionIndex, replacementValue); // Insert at specified index
    }
}
```
This function is designed to perform the task described in as few operations as possible under various conditions. The `std::find` algorithm from the STL is used for efficient searching of the target value in the vector. If found, it replaces the target value with the replacement value and if not found, inserts the replacement value at the specified index without altering the order of other elements. Edge cases are taken care of by checking whether the vector is empty or the insertion index exceeds the current size of the vector. This function minimizes memory usage and maximizes performance under various conditions.
']

