    while (node != NULL) {
        if (node->frame->qos_priority < threshold) {
            Node* next = node->next;
            remove_frame(prev, node);
            node = next;  // move to the next frame after deleting the current one.
        } else {
            prev = node;
            node = node->next;
        }
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}
```

This is a basic implementation that uses a linked list to manage MAC_FRAME structures. It locks the list while modifying it to prevent race conditions. This approach has potential performance issues if there's high contention for the lock, but in this case it seems reasonable because we have no other alternatives (like a lock-free data structure). 

