function renderFooter(scriptArray) {
    let htmlString = '<footer>';

    if (!Array.isArray(scriptArray)) {
        console.error('The input must be an array of script objects');
        return '';
    }

    for (let i = 0; i < scriptArray.length; i++) {
        const script = scriptArray[i];

        // Skip if the renderIf flag is not truthy or any required field is missing
        if (!script.renderIf || !script.identifier || !script.version) continue;

        // Create a unique id for each script by concatenating its identifier and version
        const id = `${script.identifier}-v${script.version}`;

        htmlString += `<script id="${id}" src="${script.src}"></script>`;
    }

    return htmlString + '</footer>';
}
```

This function starts by checking if the input is an array, and if not, it logs an error message and returns an empty string. Then it iterates over each script object in the array. If any required field (`renderIf`, `identifier` or `version`) is missing or the `renderIf` flag is false, it skips that script object. Otherwise, it generates a unique id for the script by combining its identifier and version, and appends a new script tag with the appropriate attributes to the HTML string. Finally, it returns the complete HTML string, enclosed within a `<footer>` tag.
