Writing such code would be a complex task that is beyond the scope of this platform due to the high level of detail and complexity involved, but I can provide you with a simplified example of how one might start structuring such a system in C. This is just an initial draft, and real implementation should involve much more considerations and complex design patterns:

```C
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <semaphore.h>
#define MAX_SIZE 100 // Define a maximum size limit for the list

typedef struct {
    int RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG;
    int RNTI;
    int CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG;
} NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T;

// Define a custom memory pool structure
typedef struct {
    sem_t semaphore; // Semaphore for synchronization
    size_t count;   // Current number of elements in the list
    size_t maxSize; // Maximum allowed size limit
    NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *list;  // Array to store the data
} MemoryPool;

// Initialize a memory pool
void initMemoryPool(MemoryPool* pool, int maxSize) {
    sem_init(&pool->semaphore, 0, 1);
    pool->count = 0;
    pool->maxSize = maxSize;
    pool->list = malloc(sizeof(NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T) * maxSize);
}

// Add an element to the memory pool
int addToMemoryPool(MemoryPool* pool, NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T item) {
    sem_wait(&pool->semaphore); // Lock access to the list

    if (pool->count >= pool->maxSize) {
        sem_post(&pool->semaphore); // Release lock before returning error code
        return -1; // Return an error code for exceeding limit
    }

    pool->list[pool->count++] = item; // Add the element

    sem_post(&pool->semaphore); // Release lock after adding element
    return 0; // Return success code
}
```
In this simple example, we have defined a `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structure and a custom memory pool `MemoryPool` to manage an array of these structures. The list is protected by a semaphore for synchronization in multithreaded environments. We also handle the case when the limit is exceeded, by returning an error code instead of adding the element.
